ection with momentum and rubber-band bounds. The draggable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"card responds to touch input via Origami’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"origami.Drag"},{"type":"text","text":" patch, which wires its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"output "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Position"},{"type":"text","text":" to the layer’s transform. When released near the center, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"card snaps back to its resting position."}],"title":"Interaction_DragView","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Interaction_DragView"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Interaction_DragView"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview","type":"topic"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction_DragView/accessibilityRotor(_:entries:)-5jrrv":{"title":"accessibilityRotor(_:entries:)","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview\/accessibilityrotor(_:entries:)-5jrrv","role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView\/accessibilityRotor(_:entries:)-5jrrv","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"accessibilityRotor"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Content"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI24AccessibilitySystemRotorV","text":"AccessibilitySystemRotor"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"entries"},{"kind":"text","text":": () -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Content"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI4ViewP","text":"View"}]},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","title":"Swami","url":"\/documentation\/swami","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"code":".origami","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example."}],"type":"topic","role":"collection"}}}